---
// Overrides Starlight's default Head to inject:
// 1. One page-specific CSS tweak: /vue/features gets a wider content
//    column, at your explicit request — its own Feature/Status table
//    wraps awkwardly at Starlight's default reading width.
// 2. A section-specific Open Graph / Twitter preview image (Vue pages
//    get one badged "Vue", Core pages one badged "Core", everything
//    else the plain site-wide default) — real per-section identity
//    for shared links, rather than one identical static image on every
//    page regardless of section.
// 3. Real, contextual JSON-LD structured data — a `TechArticle` using
//    each hand-written page's own real title/description (from
//    `Astro.props`, the same real frontmatter Starlight's own default
//    Head.astro reads) for guide/concept/example pages, a
//    `SoftwareSourceCode` block only on the three top-level overview
//    pages, and nothing extra at all on the auto-generated API
//    reference pages (`/core/api/reference/**` — thin, mostly a name
//    and a type signature, not worth describing with a generic schema
//    that adds nothing page-specific).
//
// Reads `Astro.props`, not `Astro.locals.starlightRoute` — same reason
// as this project's other overrides (Sidebar.astro): the actual
// installed @astrojs/starlight version here is 0.30.6 (confirmed via
// its own default Head.astro source in node_modules, matching KDL's own
// real Head.astro override, which documents the identical version-gap
// rationale in full).
import Default from '@astrojs/starlight/components/Head.astro';

const isVueFeaturesPage = Astro.url.pathname === `/vue/features`;

const SITE = 'https://kcw.winnem.tech';
const { entry } = Astro.props;
const pageData = entry?.data;
const pathname = Astro.url.pathname;

const isVueSection = pathname.startsWith('/vue');
const isCoreSection = pathname.startsWith('/core');
const ogImage = isVueSection ? `${SITE}/og-image-vue.png` : isCoreSection ? `${SITE}/og-image-core.png` : `${SITE}/og-image.png`;

const isOverviewPage = pathname === '/vue/' || pathname === '/core/' || pathname === '/vue' || pathname === '/core';
const isApiReferencePage = pathname.includes('/core/api/reference/');

const softwareSourceCodeJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'SoftwareSourceCode',
  name: 'Keystone Chart.js Wrappers',
  description:
    'Idiomatic Chart.js wrapper components for Vue 3, React, and Angular, sharing a single framework-agnostic core.',
  codeRepository: 'https://github.com/gwinnem/keystone-chartjs-wrappers',
  programmingLanguage: 'TypeScript',
  license: 'https://github.com/gwinnem/keystone-chartjs-wrappers/blob/main/LICENSE',
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Geirr Winnem' },
};

const techArticleJsonLd =
  pageData && !isOverviewPage && !isApiReferencePage
    ? {
        '@context': 'https://schema.org',
        '@type': 'TechArticle',
        headline: pageData.title,
        description: pageData.description,
        url: `${SITE}${pathname}`,
        author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Geirr Winnem' },
      }
    : null;
---

<Default {...Astro.props}><slot /></Default>
{isVueFeaturesPage && (
  <style is:global>
    :root {
      --sl-content-width: calc(45rem + 150px);
    }
  </style>
)}
<meta property="og:image" content={ogImage} />
<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
<meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
<meta name="twitter:image" content={ogImage} />
{isOverviewPage && (
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(softwareSourceCodeJsonLd)} />
)}
{techArticleJsonLd && (
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(techArticleJsonLd)} />
)}
